        <initializer>= &quot;_LLVM_Scalarize_&quot;</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Prefix for internal name redirection for vector function that tells the compiler to scalarize the call using the scalar name of the function. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For example, a mangled name like <computeroutput>_ZGV_LLVM_N2v_foo(_LLVM_Scalarize_foo)</computeroutput> would tell the vectorizer to vectorize the scalar call <computeroutput>foo</computeroutput>, and to scalarize it once vectorization is done. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
